peechless after thief’s mom shows up at his food truck]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129961720.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Twitch streamer in Baltimore, Musa_usa, experienced theft from his tip jar. Days later, the perpetrator's mother visited his food truck. She apologized and returned the stolen money. Musa_usa was touched by her honesty and responsibility. The incident highlights making amends and doing the right thing. The mother's actions brought a peaceful resolution to the situation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/twitch-streamer-musa_usa-left-speechless-after-thiefs-mom-shows-up-at-his-food-truck/articleshow/129961720.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/twitch-streamer-musa_usa-left-speechless-after-thiefs-mom-shows-up-at-his-food-truck/articleshow/129961720.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-02T01:30:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sumit Roy</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129961723,imgsize-516342.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[$20 million scam at 30,000 feet: Everest guides accused of poisoning trekkers for insurance payouts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129961703.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Nepal's tourism industry is embroiled in a $20 million insurance fraud scandal involving Mount Everest trekking routes. Authorities have charged 32 individuals, including guides and medical staff, for allegedly inducing illness in tourists and orchestrating unnecessary emergency evacuations for financial gain. This case raises critical questions about oversight and safety in the region.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.