-of-story-on-secret-life/articleshow/129961050.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/today-is-not-the-day-kristi-noems-husband-says-he-will-reveal-his-side-of-story-on-secret-life/articleshow/129961050.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-02T00:31:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129961128,imgsize-42760.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Innocent man awarded $975,000 after being mistakenly held in psychiatric hospital for years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/129959417.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Joshua Spriestersbach, misidentified as a criminal he did not commit, spent over two years in a Hawaii psychiatric hospital. Despite multiple chances to correct the error, authorities continued to hold him. A lawsuit filed by Spriestersbach, cited by the New York Post, led to a $975,000 settlement, with an additional $200,000 possible from the state to resolve related legal claims.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/innocent-man-awarded-975000-after-being-mistakenly-held-in-psychiatric-hospital-for-years/articleshow/129959417.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/innocent-man-awarded-975000-after-being-mistakenly-held-in-psychiatric-hospital-for-years/articleshow/129959417.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-04-01T23:50:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Trending Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-129960120,imgsize-698783.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[MrBeast $2 billion earnings claim by Agent00 sparks debate as xQc questions massive $103 million monthly figure]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align